      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1488",
      "html": "<p>Erethistoides sicula Ng, 2005, the Cheetah Catfish (family Sisoridae). Size: 39 mm SL. It differs from both E. montana and E. pipri in having a longer caudal peduncle and shorter pectoral spine. The species name comes from the Latin sicula, meaning dagger, in reference to its short pectoral spines. IUCN Red List: Data Deficient (last assessed 2009).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1488",
      "html": "<p>Asia: known from the Mansai River drainage, itself a tributary of the Brahmaputra River in northern West Bengal state in India. Type locality: Schutunga River, tributary of Mansai River, at Ansole, 26°22'24''N, 89°11'17''E, West Bengal, India.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1488",
      "html": "<p>This species lives in wide expanses of moderate flowing, shallow water over sandy substrate.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
